WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.988
Here's the chain end to end, as Microsoft's
Oracle tutorial and Book 03 describe it.

2
00:00:05.988 --> 00:00:12.299
It starts in Oracle Fusion Cloud HCM,
the HR system Oracle runs as a service.

3
00:00:12.299 --> 00:00:15.063
HCM means human capital management.

4
00:00:15.063 --> 00:00:18.254
Changes leave Fusion as
extracts, or as Atom feeds,

5
00:00:18.254 --> 00:00:22.224
which are lists of recent changes
that another program polls.

6
00:00:22.224 --> 00:00:25.212
In this pattern, the
middleware pulls from Oracle.

7
00:00:25.212 --> 00:00:27.574
The middleware is the
program in the middle.

8
00:00:27.574 --> 00:00:32.470
Microsoft says it can run in Oracle
Integration Cloud, called OIC,

9
00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:37.637
or in Azure as an Azure Function, a
Logic App, or a Data Factory pipeline.

10
00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:42.575
It turns HR records into a standard
format called SCIM and posts them to

11
00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:47.513
Microsoft Graph, Microsoft's main API,
at an endpoint called bulkUpload.

12
00:00:47.513 --> 00:00:50.801
That's Entra's API-driven
inbound provisioning.

13
00:00:50.801 --> 00:00:54.962
The Entra provisioning service then
writes the user into Entra ID.

14
00:00:54.962 --> 00:00:57.756
For users who still live
in Active Directory,

15
00:00:57.756 --> 00:01:01.758
it hands the change to a provisioning
agent: a small service on an

16
00:01:01.758 --> 00:01:06.516
on-premises server that makes outbound
connections only, and writes into AD.

17
00:01:06.516 --> 00:01:11.575
Lifecycle Workflows then run joiner and
leaver tasks on the hire and leave dates.

18
00:01:11.575 --> 00:01:13.625
Notice the DNS pattern.

19
00:01:13.625 --> 00:01:17.237
Every arrow in the top row
crosses a vendor's public name.

20
00:01:17.237 --> 00:01:21.125
Only the agent-to-AD
hop needs internal DNS.

21
00:01:21.125 --> 00:01:28.431
Sources: Microsoft Learn: Configure Oracle
HCM for automatic user provisioning [S1],

22
00:01:28.431 --> 00:01:35.419
Perform bulkUpload [S5], On-premises
application provisioning architecture [S6

23
00:01:35.419 --> 00:01:41.878
(excerpt)], Plan cloud HR application to
Entra user provisioning [S8 (excerpt)],

24
00:01:41.878 --> 00:01:46.855
Lifecycle workflows attribute
sync [S11 (excerpt)]; Oracle,

25
00:01:46.855 --> 00:01:52.010
Working with Atom [S18]; Book
03 Ch05, Provisioning Services.
